Package: steam-arm-setup
Version: 2.0
Section: games
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: bash (>= 5.0), python3 (>= 3.8), curl, ca-certificates, xz-utils
Recommends: whiptail
Maintainer: Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: install Valve's native ARM64 Steam client
 Installs Valve's native ARM64 Steam client and supporting pieces:
 FEX-Emu, x86-64 Ubuntu 24.04 RootFS with Mesa for Valve's emulation
 tool (graphics provider), launcher, and optional
 components such as a Vulkan compatibility layer, joystick and
 controller access rules, and a desktop menu entry.
 .
 Nothing is downloaded during package installation. All downloads
 happen when the steam-arm-setup command is run.
 .
 Requires an ARM64 Debian or Ubuntu family system with a working
 Vulkan driver.
